From a4fff01f2ae12217b16aff355395eab5ccf1e6d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] x86/k1om: build the 6.18 code base with the MPSS k1om
 toolchain

The only toolchain that targets k1om is the MPSS 3.8.6 one: gcc 5.1.1
and binutils 2.22.52. Everything here keeps the 6.18 sources compiling
and assembling with it; all of it is dead on KNC at run time (guarded
by CONFIG_X86_EARLYMIC/MK1OM or by CPU features KNC never has).

gcc 5.1.1:
 - It accepts the "=@cc<cond>" asm flag-output constraint but does not
   implement it (no __GCC_ASM_FLAG_OUTPUTS__): the "output" is a stale
   register, so every try_cmpxchg(), test_and_set_bit() etc. returned
   garbage. First victim was the mutex unlock at the end of
   cgroup_init_subsys(), whose slow path retried a "failed" cmpxchg
   forever, hanging the card before its first printk. CC_SET()/CC_OUT()
   are restored in asm/asm.h with the setcc fallback and the 30
   flag-output sites (cmpxchg*, rmwcc, bitops, percpu, uaccess, signal,
   archrandom, special_insns, sev, boot/) use them again.
 - min-tool-version: gcc floor 5.1, binutils floor 2.22.
 - objtool is not built for EARLYMIC (it cannot decode VPU code and its
   libsubcmd needs a newer host gcc), so the !CONFIG_OBJTOOL asm side
   needs STACK_FRAME_NON_STANDARD_FP; static calls use the out-of-line
   trampolines.
 - 6.15 forces -march=x86-64 for 64-bit builds, which makes the k1om
   gcc emit cmov: MK1OM keeps the compiler default.

binutils 2.22 (no mnemonics for anything after ~2011):
 - mfence/lfence: FENCE_SWAPGS_*, FILL_RETURN_BUFFER, clear_bhb_loop
   and the entry_64 GS fence are empty/skipped (in-order core, no RSB).
 - rd/wr{fs,gs}base, rdrand/rdseed, invpcid, xgetbv/xsetbv, rdtscp,
   rdpid, monitor/mwait(x), clflushopt/clwb, pause, tzcnt, cmova,
   movnti/sfence, vmmcall, clac/stac and the XSAVE family are stubbed,
   given a .byte encoding or replaced by the plain form (rep bsf,
   branch instead of cmova, mov instead of movnti, memcpy for
   memcpy_flushcache); XSAVE/XRSTOR are ud2 (KNC has no XSAVE).
 - U/UL suffixes in asm expressions are rejected: verify_cpu.S masks
   (never run on KNC) and the uprobe trampoline alignment.
 - The SSE2/AVX/SHA-NI/PCLMUL asm of the 6.17 lib/crc and lib/crypto
   libraries and the vDSO chacha getrandom (6.11) are not built;
   XMM/XMM2 and CMOV are not required features; the microcode loader
   (reads IA32_UCODE_REV) and 128-bit cmpxchg (no CX16) are off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
